<?xml version="1.0" encoding="UTF-8"?>

<subsection xml:id="sec-14-assignment-summary-6week">
  <title>Assignment Summary</title>

  <p>
    This six-week calendar provides a pacing guide for MATH 1314. Always verify exact
    due dates and submission requirements in Canvas and ALEKS.
  </p>

  <list>
    <title>Six-Week Calendar</title>
    <ol>
      <li>
        <p><em>Week 1:</em> Course orientation, syllabus review, ALEKS setup, and first homework set.</p>
      </li>
      <li>
        <p><em>Week 2:</em> Continue core algebra topics, complete ALEKS objectives, and submit assigned writing/check-in tasks.</p>
      </li>
      <li>
        <p><em>Week 3:</em> Complete weekly ALEKS work, participate in required discussions, and begin preparing for the first major assessment.</p>
      </li>
      <li>
        <p><em>Week 4:</em> Take the scheduled assessment, continue new content, and stay current on ALEKS assignments.</p>
      </li>
      <li>
        <p><em>Week 5:</em> Focus on higher-level topics, complete remaining writing/discussion tasks, and begin cumulative review.</p>
      </li>
      <li>
        <p><em>Week 6:</em> Finish all ALEKS and course assignments, complete final assessments, and submit any required end-of-course work.</p>
      </li>
    </ol>
  </list>

  <p>
    Because summer deadlines move quickly, plan ahead and work daily whenever possible.
  </p>
</subsection>
